<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ommelanden</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Groninger Ommelanden</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Ommelanden are the rural Frisian districts surrounding the city of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/groningen">Groningen</a> in the northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-the-netherlands">Netherlands</a>. In the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/middle-ages">Middle Ages</a> they were self-governing farming communities that the city sought to dominate through its staple rights and courts. From 1594 city and countryside formed the province of Stad en Lande within the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch-republic">Dutch Republic</a>, a union marked by long quarrels, and the area is now part of the province of Groningen.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ommelanden.jpg" alt="Ommelanden" width="320" height="311" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: T.Bosse · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Groningenhistorisch.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
